# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# haruyuki-gui -- repository ignore rules
#
# Two invariants this file must never break:
#   1. /docs/ and /_research/ are internal-only. docs/ carries its own nested
#      .git, so ignoring it also keeps git from recording an embedded
#      repository in the index.
#   2. fixtures/ and pnpm-lock.yaml MUST be committed. Never add a rule that
#      matches them (no bare `*`, no `*.lock`, no `*.yaml`).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Internal-only material (root-anchored on purpose) ---------------------
/docs/
/_research/
# Internal tooling that hard-codes host names and addresses. The design is in
# docs/46 (also internal), so the file stays on the operator's machine rather
# than in the repository the project is published from.
#
# remote-clean deletes a directory on that same machine. It carries no address
# either, but publishing it would still be wrong: an outside reader cannot tell
# from the file that it is written for one operator's peer, and a script whose
# whole job is `rmdir /s /q` reads as a general-purpose tool right up until it
# is pointed somewhere else. Keeping it beside remote-verify keeps the pair
# honest - both are operator-local, and neither pretends to be portable.
/scripts/remote-verify.mjs
/scripts/remote-clean.mjs

# --- Dependencies ----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.pnpm-debug.log

# --- Build output ----------------------------------------------------------
dist/
out/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.tgz

# --- Test and coverage artifacts -------------------------------------------
coverage/
.vitest/
*.lcov

# --- Tool caches -----------------------------------------------------------
.eslintcache
.prettiercache
.cache/
.tmp/

# --- Logs ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
pnpm-debug.log*
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
report.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.json

# --- Editor / IDE state (personal config only) -----------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- OS metadata -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
ehthumbs.db

# --- Local environment / secrets -------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.local
_acceptance/

# --- G1 packaged runtime staging -------------------------------------------
/apps/desktop/runtime/
/apps/desktop/runtime-lock.json
/apps/desktop/release/

# --- handoff: development accident dumps, read then deleted ---------------
# Written by a leader when it stops, read by whoever takes over, deleted after.
# Deliberately not versioned: these are transcripts of what went wrong during
# development, not project artifacts. A committed handoff would outlive the
# accident it describes and read like documentation.
/handoff/
